  "question": {
    "text": "A plane <math><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> passing through the point <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>&nbsp;is perpendicular to the planes&nbsp;<math><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></math> and <math><mn>3</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>z</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo></math> If the distance of the point <math><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>1,2</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfenced></math> from the plane <math><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> is <math><mi>k</mi></math>&nbsp;units, then the value of&nbsp;<math><mn>34</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"></mi><msup><mrow><mi>k</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math> is equal to",
